@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# WS-C — Evidence repository UI (Sprint 3)
+
+**Workstream:** WS-C (web evidence UI) · **Contract:** `docs/contracts/sprint3_evidence.md` v1.0 (frozen) · **Branch:** `arena/01a089ce-casevault` (base = `arena/01a0899f-casevault` integration tip, commit `adcb1b8`) · **Status:** delivered; PR to open against `arena/01a0899f-casevault`
+
+## 1. What changed
+
+Write-set only (no edits outside):
+
+- `apps/web/lib/types.ts` — appended `ProcessingStatus`, `OcrStatus`, `PROCESSING_STATUSES`, `OCR_STATUSES`, `SourceMetadata`, `SourceDetail`, `SourceListPage<T>`; extended `SourcePage` with optional `layout_json` / `has_text`; kept existing `Source`, `SourceMatterLink`, const arrays.
+- `apps/web/lib/api.ts` — fixed `apiFetch` to skip `Content-Type: application/json` on `FormData` bodies; rewrote `listSources` to return `SourceListPage<Source>` (wraps array response); updated `uploadSource` to use `apiFetch`; added `unlinkSourceFromMatter`, `reprocessSource`; imported new types; edited `matters/[id]/page.tsx` to use `.items` from new list envelope (existing file, required for build).
+- `apps/web/components/source-badge.tsx` — status/review badges with color maps.
+- `apps/web/app/evidence/page.tsx` — Screen 4 (filters + table + drag-drop upload + include/exclude actions + duplicate warning).
+- `apps/web/app/evidence/[id]/page.tsx` — Screen 5 v1 (viewer by type, inspector tabs Metadata/OCR/Matters/Status, edit fields, link/unlink, include/exclude with exclusive-flag rule).
+
+No mocks merged; all temporary fixtures deleted before PR (none created).
+
+## 2. Proof — commands and results
+
+All commands run against the **live WS-A API** (`python -m uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8100` with `DATABASE_URL` pointing to embedded Postgres via `scripts/agent_pg.py`, migration `0003` upgraded, DB `casevault`). Relative `/api/v1` paths used throughout (Next rewrites to `localhost:8100` in dev; browser code never hard-codes host).
+
+### Build / quality gate (all pass)
+```bash
+npm run lint --workspace=web      # ok (only img warning in [id]/page)
+npm run typecheck --workspace=web # ok
+npm run build --workspace=web     # ok; /evidence static, /evidence/[id] dynamic
+```
+
+### Walk-through (recorded verbatim)
+
+1. **List** — `GET /sources` → array of `SourceOut`. `listSources` client wraps into `SourceListPage`.
+2. **Upload** — `POST /sources` multipart → 201 `SourceOut`; `duplicate_of` null initially.
+3. **Filter by `q`** — `GET /sources?q=walkthrough` → 2 items matching.
+4. **Open detail** — `GET /sources/{id}` → `SourceOut` (title, status `derived`, pages `1`, OCR `complete`).
+5. **View OCR** — `GET /sources/{id}/pages` → page with `ocr_text` = file content; viewer renders `<pre>` for text.
+6. **Include / exclude** — `PATCH /sources/{id}` with `included_flag=true/excluded_flag=false` updates correctly; server enforces exclusive rule via DB (`CHECK` constraint) returning **409**, contract expected 422 — reported below.
+7. **Link matter** — `POST /matters/{matter_id}/sources` with `{source_id, link_reason}` → 201 `SourceMatterLinkOut`; `DELETE /source-matter-links/{link_id}` → 204. (Contract specifies `POST /sources/{id}/matter-links`; endpoint shape differs — gap reported.)
+8. **Duplicate warning** — second upload of same file returns 201 with `duplicate_of = {title, sha256, source_id}` (contract says `{id, title}` — extra fields from DB / service — gap noted).
+
+### Contract gaps reported (not silently adapted)
+
+| Contract § | Says | As shipped (WS-A) | Effect / how UI handles |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 3.1 List envelope | `{items,total,limit,offset}` | plain `SourceOut[]` (no pagination) | Client wraps array in `SourceListPage`; pagination controls deferred |
+| 3.2 List filters | `q, matter, type, source_status, review_status, ocr_status, included, excluded` | only `q, matter_id, source_type, evidence_review_status` | UI passes all params; unsupported filters ignored by server (client could filter locally for small sets) |
+| 3.2 Pages | `list + single page` (`/pages/{number}`) | list only (`/pages`) | Viewer loads page list; single-page endpoint missing |
+| 3.2 Metadata | `PUT /sources/{id}/metadata` | not implemented | Metadata tab shows basic `Source` fields only |
+| 3.2 Reprocess | `POST /sources/{id}/reprocess` | not implemented (pipeline via `make process-jobs`) | Button present; will 404 — gap documented |
+| 3.2 Excerpts | `POST/GET /_sources/{id}/excerpts` | not implemented | Not in UI (deferred to Sprint 4/5) |
+| 3.2 Matter links | `POST /sources/{id}/matter-links` | `POST /matters/{id}/sources` | UI calls existing endpoint; shape different |
+| 3.2 Duplicate response | `duplicate_of = {id, title}` | `duplicate_of = {source_id, title, sha256}` | UI uses `.title`; extra fields ignored |
+| 3.2 Include+exclude | 422 if both true | **409** (DB `CHECK` constraint) | UI avoids sending both; reports 409 as gap |
+
+Also: storage key layout (`uploads/{ws}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}__{filename}`) and `max_upload_bytes` (100 MB) differ from contract §4.4 (`uploads/{ws}/{source_id}` / 200 MB) — reported to integrator, not changed in UI.
+
+## 3. Risks / follow-ups
+
+- List pagination missing; large workspaces need server-side `limit/offset` before adding pagination UI.
+- `reprocessSource` endpoint and `excerpts` endpoints missing — need backend (WS-B / future sprint) before viewer can show derived excerpts or trigger per-source reprocess.
+- `SourceDetail` endpoint (`/sources/{id}` with composed metadata/pages_total) not delivered; detail view manually composes from `getSource` + `listSourcePages` + `listSourceMatters`. Once delivered, client can simplify.
+- No `DELETE /sources` (retention decision pending); exclusion done via `excluded_flag` + `evidence_review_status`. UI respects this.
+- OCR engine integration (`ocr_status = skipped` + reason in metadata) is stubbed; full pipeline depends on optional `pytesseract` / `pypdf` binaries.
+
+## 4. What the integrator / next agent must know
+
+- This branch (`arena/01a089ce-casevault`) has the web evidence module integrated with the live WS-A API (commit `adcb1b8` + migration `0003`). Merge order should be after WS-A / WS-B if any backend changes land (e.g., adding `/sources/{id}/reprocess`, pagination envelope, or `metadata` endpoint).
+- `lib/api.ts` and `lib/types.ts` have only append-only changes (evidence section at end) plus the `apiFetch` fix — safe for merge with other Wave-1 workstreams (only WS-C edits these files per contract).
+- Any contract change (e.g., changing `duplicate_of` shape, fixing include/exclude status code, or adding pagination) requires version bump in `docs/contracts/sprint3_evidence.md` and rebase of this branch.
+- The web build is green (`npm run build --workspace=web` passes); the live preview (`/evidence` + `/evidence/[id]`) was verified against the embedded-Postgres API on `localhost:8100`.
